FLASK_APP=StoreApp.main              # The FLASK_APP configuration option is set to "main", which specifies the entry point of the Flask application. This tells Flask which module or file to run when starting the application. In this case, it indicates that the main application code is located in the "main.py" file.
FLASK_DEBUG=1              # The FLASK_DEBUG configuration option is set to 1, which enables the debug mode in Flask. When debug mode is enabled, the application will automatically reload when code changes are detected, and it will provide detailed error messages and stack traces in the browser when an error occurs. This is useful during development for easier debugging and testing of the application.